  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-bnpl-faq-item (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package runs a bundled dropper (_ext.js) that fingerprints the host platform/arch, downloads a second-stage binary over HTTPS from oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), and falls back to a DNS TXT-based command channel on c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru that reassembles a base64 payload from chunked TXT records. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe on Windows) and executed as a detached background process via /bin/sh -c or cmd.exe start /b, so it outlives the parent process.",
